{"TagDevice is now called synchronously in Authenticate instead of in a goroutine, which will block authentication requests if the store is slow or unavailable - the original approach had a 2-minute timeout to prevent this": 0.9283419251441956, "When count >= deviceLimit, expired devices (with updated_at older than 30 days) receive ErrDeviceLimitReached even though they don't contribute to the count, preventing them from reconnecting when the limit is at capacity": 0.8744297027587891, "AnonymousDeviceLimit is typed as int64 in Go (always serializes as a number including 0) but TypeScript type is number | undefined (implies field may be absent) - these types are inconsistent": 0.42724475264549255}